{
  "_doc": "createMedia routing and tools conformance (SPEC §7G.3, §7G.6). Each case builds test-only custom MediaClients from clients[]: name; supports(verb) = verb in verbs; args(verb) = verbs[verb].args (absent ⇒ the client declares no args(), so every canonical arg is accepted); calling a verb records {client, verb, args} and returns outcome.result, or fails with a media error {message: outcome.error, status: outcome.status} (status unavailable must use the port's typed unavailable error). Assert expectCalls exactly (order, args after nulls removed), then result / error+status, then the tool face (fresh clients). schemaCases: build createMedia(clients).tools() and assert names, order, descriptions, source and inputSchema exactly (Go: key order not asserted). emptyClients: createMedia([]) fails with exactly that message. modelParts (SPEC §7G.6 model visibility): the parts of this tool result that message assembly (§8A) emits to the model — only image parts; video/audio parts stay in RunResult.files and toolCalls[].parts only. Assert with the port's assembly function on a transcript containing this tool result.",
